WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.736
-Hello, everyone and welcome
back to the attic.

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.704
I want to start by addressing
something

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.006
because there have been some
nasty rumors online.

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:10.710
The books on my side table are
real books, with real titles,

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.845
by real authors,
and I'm not switching in

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:15.248
fake ones
over the course of the show.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:18.618
I would never, what, ask
the art department at our show

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.786
to make phony book covers
for nonexistent

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:23.556
"Thorn Bird" sequels
and have them sent here

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.659
in the mail for a bit that
all of, I want to say,

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.628
eight people tops
would even enjoy?

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.462
I mean, that would be
a colossal waste of time.

00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:32.331
And I also want to assure you
that if it was a bit,

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:33.800
which it's not,
I would stop it immediately

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.668
before it dragged out
and became unsatisfying.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:39.672
Speaking of unsatisfying --
boom, another perfect segue --

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.041
the president is declaring
victory on coronavirus

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.777
even as a whistleblower
offered damning testimony today

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:47.280
on the Trump administration's
disastrous response.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.049
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:53.919
♪♪

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:57.123
Today the House heard damning
testimony from Dr. Rick Bright,

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.158
a whistleblower who was
punished for questioning

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:01.093
the president's aggressive
advertising

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:04.897
of the unproven anti-malaria
drug hydroxychloroquine

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.332
as a treatment for coronavirus.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.834
Do you remember
hydroxychloroquine,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.236
the Furby of medical fads
for like a month?

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:13.039
Hydroxychloroquine was hotter
than CBD oil,

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.108
and it turns out
works just as well.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:18.911
Bright made clear today that his
caution on hydroxychloroquine

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:21.080
was part of the reason
he was pushed out.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.516
-I believe part of
the removal process for me

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:27.453
was initiated because
of a pushback

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:31.057
that I gave when they asked me
to put in place

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:33.892
an expanded access protocol
that would make

00:01:33.892 --> 00:01:36.929
chloroquine more freely
available to Americans

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:40.032
that were not under the close
supervision of a physician

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:41.935
and may not even be confirmed
to be infected

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.635
with the coronavirus.
-That's right,

00:01:43.635 --> 00:01:45.571
they wanted to give it out to
people who might not even

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:47.006
have had coronavirus.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.242
I wouldn't be surprised if Trump
had personally submitted

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.076
a request to travel
around the country

00:01:51.076 --> 00:01:52.578
in a windowless white van

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.780
offering loose bags
of chloroquine to kids.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.482
[ As Trump ] "You guys want to
ride the quine?

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.784
I'll meet you out back
behind the bleachers.

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:00.553
This is a tiny bag of drugs."

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.054
Bright, a vaccine expert

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.491
who led a biodefense agency
in the health department,

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.859
had a stark assessment
of just how badly

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.761
the Trump administration
had failed

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.230
in its response to
the coronavirus outbreak.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.399
-I believe we could have
done better.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.035
I believe there are
critical steps

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.937
that we did not take in time.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.506
Those alarms were not
responded to with action.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.842
-Okay, side note here,
but that is

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.277
what I want a doctor
to sound like --

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:27.146
calm, reasonable,
doesn't engage in hyperbole,

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:28.514
gives it to you straight.

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.482
Trump, of course, prefers
that his doctors sound like

00:02:30.482 --> 00:02:32.118
roadies for Metallica.

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.653
"Hey, man, I looked
at your CAT scan.

00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:37.957
Looks like you got what
we call upside-down disease.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:41.093
Anyway, you want to
ride the quine?"

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.862
Although I have to say,
probably even more shocking

00:02:43.862 --> 00:02:45.431
than that comment
was this moment

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.533
when Bright relayed
a conversation he had

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.869
about our shortage
of respirator masks.

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.438
-Congressman, I'll never
forget the e-mails I received

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:58.811
from Mike Bowen indicating
that our mask supply

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:02.815
or N-95 respirator supply
was completely decimated,

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.785
and he said,
"We're in deep [bleep]."

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.887
-Wow, you know it's bad when
someone as soft-spoken

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:10.589
as this guy drops a curse word
on live television.

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:12.558
It's like FaceTiming
with your grandma

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.293
and asking her how
her knitting is going.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:16.328
"Oh, you know, I just do it
to pass the time

00:03:16.328 --> 00:03:17.930
while I'm baking cookies.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.232
These mother [bleep]
are taking forever."

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:23.403
Bright had a damning and truly
harrowing assessment

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.170
of where we are as a nation
on everything

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.739
from vaccines to testing.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.175
And he warned that
if we don't put together

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.709
a national strategy now,

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:32.911
things could be very bleak
come the fall.

00:03:32.911 --> 00:03:34.380
-Without better planning,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.884
2020 could be the darkest
winter in modern history.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.052
The truth must be based
on science.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:44.023
We have the world's greatest
scientists, let us lead.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:47.126
Let us speak without fear
of retribution.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.762
There are things we must
do immediately.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:53.332
We must increase the public
education about the basics --

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:55.701
washing hands,
social distancing,

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.670
appropriate face covering.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.272
-Of course, as he was
watching that,

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.340
there was a good chance Trump
was sneezing into his hands,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.541
surrounded by reporters

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:04.276
and wearing a face mask
over his eyes.

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:06.545
"If I can't see you,
I can't give you the corona."

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:08.414
Instead of listening to Bright

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.983
and taking his warnings
seriously,

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.484
Trump was on Fox News
this morning,

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.986
bragging about the one thing
he always brags about,

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.056
the China travel ban
he imposed in late January.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.824
The "New York Times"
reported last month

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:22.095
that 430,000 people have
traveled from China to the U.S.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.863
since coronavirus surfaced.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:26.765
But that hasn't stopped Trump
from saying stuff like this...

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:30.203
-In January, I put -- and I
was criticized by everybody,

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:33.205
including Dr. Fauci,
I put in a wall.

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:34.807
We put in a very strong wall.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:37.310
-There's a good chance Trump
thinks they built a literal wall

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.911
between the U.S. and China.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.480
"We built a wall in the Pacific
keeping out immigrants,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.783
manatees, sharks, and whales.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:46.018
Unfortunately, we've had
less trouble, less success,

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:47.787
I should say,
stopping dolphins,

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.855
what with all the tricks they've
learned at SeaWorld.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:51.657
SeaWorld, of course,
a water park

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:54.493
that thrived under Obama.

00:04:54.493 --> 00:04:56.195
So, if we're pointing
fingers..."

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:57.930
The frustrating thing
about listening

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.531
to Dr. Bright's testimony
is that everything

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:00.733
he's talking about is possible,

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.067
as we've seen
from other countries.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.702
Throughout this crisis,
Americans have watched

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:06.305
as countries across the world,
from Germany to Australia,

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.874
New Zealand to Taiwan
successfully contained

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:11.377
and suppressed their coronavirus
outbreaks

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:15.348
and began to safely and slowly
reopen their economies.

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:17.050
Meanwhile, here in the U.S.,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:20.252
things are so bad, we have
senators showing up to hearings

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:22.121
like outlaw highwaymen,

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.690
drinking alone
in the corner of a salon.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.493
Tim Kaine,
what happened to you?

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:30.430
You went from vice presidential
nominee to divorced dad

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.031
who forgot it was Halloween.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:35.334
Although, I honestly do wish
this Tim Kaine

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.302
had been Hillary Clinton's
running mate.

00:05:37.302 --> 00:05:38.537
Instead of debating Mike Pence,

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.339
he would have challenged him
to a dual.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:44.643
"Hey, Mike Pence, how about you
Pokémon -- go to hell."

00:05:44.643 --> 00:05:46.479
Pow-pow!

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.948
Insanely good mime work today.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.816
You guys remember the quine?

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:53.051
Although, I will give him credit
for at least wearing a mask,

00:05:53.051 --> 00:05:54.954
unlike some of his
Republican colleagues,

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.822
who have decided to
turn mask wearing,

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:59.291
a proven technique
for eliminating transmission

00:05:59.291 --> 00:06:01.761
of respiratory illnesses,
into yet another

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:03.429
dumb culture war issue.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.597
Like Louisiana Senator
John Kennedy,

00:06:05.597 --> 00:06:07.966
who said this bizarre thing
on Fox News.

00:06:07.966 --> 00:06:10.936
-I don't want to have to wear
a face mask in the shower.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:12.938
-Okay, so don't.
I think are you're safe.

00:06:12.938 --> 00:06:15.007
I doubt anybody would want to be
within six feet of you

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.375
when you're naked and wet.

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:18.710
No one's telling you to wear
a face mask in the shower.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.446
Although, based on
voice alone,

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.081
if anyone sounds like
they should be wearing

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:25.651
a Tim Kaine-style bandana,
it's this Douche of Hazzard.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.620
Seriously, can we just
make stuff up

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.455
and then
get angry about it now?

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:32.525
"And another thing, I don't want
these crazy libs telling me

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:35.461
to wear socks on my hands
and a bucket on my chin.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.996
I mean, I'll do it
for public health,

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:39.064
but I won't be
happy about it."

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:41.367
You only need to wear a mask
when you're out,

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.936
around other people, or when you
can't socially distance.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.371
I mean, where are you taking
your showers?

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:47.640
Are you secretly
a Starship Trooper?

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:50.509
Underrated film. If you want to
catch up on that one,

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:52.044
this is a good time to do it.

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.745
Mask wearing
is a simple technique

00:06:53.745 --> 00:06:55.213
that's been proven to
reduce the transmission

00:06:55.213 --> 00:06:56.715
of respiratory illnesses,

00:06:56.715 --> 00:06:58.884
and it's been adopted widely
in countries that have

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:00.720
successfully contained or
suppressed their outbreaks.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.055
Like South Korea, which had
their first confirmed case

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:04.456
on the same day we had ours.

00:07:04.456 --> 00:07:06.926
South Korea successfully
contained their outbreak

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.528
early on, and they did it with
massive nationwide testing.

00:07:09.528 --> 00:07:11.997
It wasn't just widespread,
it was early.

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:13.566
At the beginning of March,
for example,

00:07:13.566 --> 00:07:15.601
when it was reported that fewer
than 500 people had been tested

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:18.837
here in the U.S.,
in South Korea, they already had

00:07:18.837 --> 00:07:22.340
drive-thru setups, where
anyone could get tested safely

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:25.110
without leaving their car
and receive their results back

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:26.511
in a few days.

00:07:26.511 --> 00:07:28.180
I know if you told Trump
other countries were beating us

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.748
on tests, he wouldn't care,
but if you told him

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:31.617
other countries were beating
were beating us on drive-thrus,

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.385
we would have had
this problem solved ASAP.

00:07:33.385 --> 00:07:35.454
"Today I'm invoking
the Defense Protection Act

00:07:35.454 --> 00:07:37.456
to immediately ramp up
our nation's supply

00:07:37.456 --> 00:07:41.761
of masks, Frosty, Whoppers,
apple pies.

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:44.296
And I'm proud to announce today
that thanks to the efforts

00:07:44.296 --> 00:07:46.999
of our search,
the McRib is back.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:48.800
The one curve you don't want
to flatten."

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.736
And by the way, that doesn't
mean coronavirus

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:53.105
just disappeared forever
in South Korea.

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.374
In fact, they just had to
reimpose some lockdown measures

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.842
after a resurgence of cases.

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.344
But that tells us two things --

00:07:58.344 --> 00:08:00.145
one, you can't just
reopen the economy

00:08:00.145 --> 00:08:02.414
without expecting that
outbreaks reoccur.

00:08:02.414 --> 00:08:05.284
And two, you need an aggressive
regime of testing,

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:06.852
tracing, and isolation.

00:08:06.852 --> 00:08:08.120
If we had that here,

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.889
everyone would feel
much more comfortable

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:11.823
knowing that if we went
back to work,

00:08:11.823 --> 00:08:13.458
and there was another outbreak,

00:08:13.458 --> 00:08:15.595
we'd detect it early
and respond quickly.

00:08:15.595 --> 00:08:17.396
Instead, we have senators
dressing like

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:19.899
NPCs in "Red Dead Redemption,"

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:21.600
and others complaining
that mask wearing

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.536
is ruining their nightly
bubble bath.

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:25.371
"I'd like to sit in my tub.

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:27.473
And I'd blow bubbles,
but I can't do that

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:30.242
'cause I have to wear a mask to
avoid spreading coronavirus

00:08:30.242 --> 00:08:32.077
to my ducky."

00:08:32.077 --> 00:08:33.813
Now, South Korea set up
their drive-thru testing

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:35.014
in February.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.116
By mid-March, Trump
announced his own plan

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:38.751
to expand drive-thru testing,

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:41.954
but he decided to rely on
private companies instead,

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:44.456
and did his usual schtick
where he calls them up

00:08:44.456 --> 00:08:46.592
one by one to talk about
how great they are.

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:49.562
-We've been in discussions
with pharmacies and retailers

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:52.631
to make drive-thru tests
available

00:08:52.631 --> 00:08:54.533
in the critical locations

00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:57.236
identified by public
health professionals.

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:59.671
One of them is Doug McMillon
from Walmart.

00:08:59.671 --> 00:09:02.741
And I'd like to have Doug,
if you would, say a few words.

00:09:02.741 --> 00:09:04.677
And, Richard, if you could
come up, please.

00:09:04.677 --> 00:09:07.613
Richard, please.
Walgreens.

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:10.115
Brian Cornell.
Target.

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:11.783
Is Tom here?
Tom Polen?

00:09:11.783 --> 00:09:14.286
And Matt Sauce, please,
of Roche.

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:17.490
David Pierre of Signify --
Signify Health.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:20.159
Adam Schechter, who's really
been of tremendous help,

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:21.560
LabCorp, please.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:25.264
Thomas Moriarty, CVS.
We all know CVS.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:27.800
-"Duane and Reade
from Duane Reade.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.168
Thank you both for making it.

00:09:29.168 --> 00:09:33.439
Matthias Mickelberry,
CEO of M&amp;Ms, great work.

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:36.041
Long John Silver,
right over there.

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:38.677
We all know Long John.
Thar he blows, right over there.

00:09:38.677 --> 00:09:40.312
The Taco Bell chihuahua.

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:42.047
What's that?

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:43.849
He's not in his box?

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:45.684
Well, you have to think
outside the box.

00:09:45.684 --> 00:09:47.252
Or just find him.

00:09:47.252 --> 00:09:50.089
Why? Because yo quiero him
to be here.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:52.858
The Noid? Where's the Noid?
Right over there.

00:09:52.858 --> 00:09:56.262
It would break my heart
if I avoided the Noid.

00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:58.730
I think this -- has this bit
gone on long enough?

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:00.799
Oh, Little Ceasars pizza.

00:10:00.799 --> 00:10:03.101
You know, a lot of people --
a lot of people think

00:10:03.101 --> 00:10:04.970
he's saying, 'pizza, pizza,'
but not me.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:08.473
I know it's 'Pizza. Pizza.'

00:10:08.473 --> 00:10:09.875
Coppertone baby.
Where's the Coppertone --

00:10:09.875 --> 00:10:11.143
Where is she?
She can't get up

00:10:11.143 --> 00:10:13.078
because the dog has her
swimsuit in its mouth?

00:10:13.078 --> 00:10:15.281
Is it the Taco Bell dog?
Well, why don't you check?"

00:10:15.281 --> 00:10:17.115
So, that was mid-March.

00:10:17.115 --> 00:10:19.051
I think that was the right
amount of time to do that.

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:20.619
Already far too late to begin
scaling up tests.

00:10:20.619 --> 00:10:22.788
Again, it came after a testing
debacle at the CDC

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:25.991
that significantly slowed
our response, but still,

00:10:25.991 --> 00:10:27.459
it was a promising initiative,

00:10:27.459 --> 00:10:29.528
if it could get up
and run in quickly.

00:10:29.528 --> 00:10:32.264
Instead, a month after
Trump's announcement,

00:10:32.264 --> 00:10:34.066
"Business Insider"
found only eight sites

00:10:34.066 --> 00:10:36.134
were operating among
three of the companies,

00:10:36.134 --> 00:10:38.237
the fourth Walgreens wasn't able
to open the first batch

00:10:38.237 --> 00:10:41.340
of its promised 15 locations
until April 17th,

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.375
Target opened only one site,

00:10:43.375 --> 00:10:45.410
and appears to have dropped out
of the effort.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:46.845
And if you go to CVS,

00:10:46.845 --> 00:10:49.080
they just decided to stop having
employees altogether.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.650
Actually, all CVSs are
technically drive-thrus

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.652
and that you could literally
drive through one

00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:55.321
and there would be no one
there to stop you.

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:57.589
This is why we need
an actual functioning

00:10:57.589 --> 00:11:00.459
centralized federal government
that listens to scientists

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:02.328
instead of just relying on
private companies

00:11:02.328 --> 00:11:04.195
to do things that don't benefit
their investors

00:11:04.195 --> 00:11:05.397
or their bottom lines.

00:11:05.397 --> 00:11:07.333
Republicans love to hollow out
the government

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:08.967
and outsource everything
to big business

00:11:08.967 --> 00:11:10.936
and then complain
the government is incompetent

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:12.304
and should be run like
a business.

00:11:12.304 --> 00:11:14.740
That's their scam --
make government incompetent,

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:18.043
then use that incompetence as
proof that government is bad.

00:11:18.043 --> 00:11:19.811
They're like a husband who
cheats on his wife and says,

00:11:19.811 --> 00:11:23.082
"See, this is proof
we need an open marriage."

00:11:23.082 --> 00:11:24.883
In fact, Republicans
are now arguing

00:11:24.883 --> 00:11:26.685
that nonpartisan public health
officials,

00:11:26.685 --> 00:11:28.353
like Dr. Anthony Fauci,
the nation's leading

00:11:28.353 --> 00:11:31.223
infectious disease expert,
shouldn't be allowed

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:32.524
to make decisions about

00:11:32.524 --> 00:11:33.792
the government's
coronavirus response.

00:11:33.792 --> 00:11:35.293
-I think
the one-size-fits-all,

00:11:35.293 --> 00:11:36.729
that we're going to have
a national strategy

00:11:36.729 --> 00:11:39.398
and nobody's going to go
to school is kind of ridiculous.

00:11:39.398 --> 00:11:41.934
So I think we ought to have
a little bit of humility

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:45.570
in our belief that we know
what's best for the economy.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.305
And as much as I respect you,
Dr. Fauci,

00:11:47.305 --> 00:11:49.041
I don't think
you're the end-all.

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:50.375
I don't think you're
the one person

00:11:50.375 --> 00:11:51.810
that gets to make a decision.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.345
-No one said he was.

00:11:53.345 --> 00:11:55.481
He wasn't even the one person
at that hearing.

00:11:55.481 --> 00:11:58.383
There were four top public
health officials who testified,

00:11:58.383 --> 00:12:00.486
including FDA Commissioner
Stephen Hahn,

00:12:00.486 --> 00:12:03.989
who Skyped in, I'm guessing,
from the finale of "Lost"?

00:12:03.989 --> 00:12:05.990
"I am going to try to keep
my answers brief,

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.759
as I may be a ghost."

00:12:07.759 --> 00:12:10.295
Also, as Fauci pointed out,
all he does

00:12:10.295 --> 00:12:12.731
is offer advice
as a doctor and public official.

00:12:12.731 --> 00:12:15.667
He often corrects himself
or amends his judgments

00:12:15.667 --> 00:12:16.836
based on new information,

00:12:16.836 --> 00:12:18.870
and he doesn't make
any policy decisions.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:21.740
Yet they're acting like he's
somehow a puppet master

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.775
controlling an otherwise
powerless Trump.

00:12:23.775 --> 00:12:25.344
Trump's the president.

00:12:25.344 --> 00:12:27.445
He's supposed to be the one who
makes all the actual decisions.

00:12:27.445 --> 00:12:29.781
And yet, in their all-consuming
attempts to cover

00:12:29.781 --> 00:12:31.450
for the president's failures,
they've been casting about

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.886
for someone else to blame,

00:12:33.886 --> 00:12:36.054
and they've apparently landed
on Fauci.

00:12:36.054 --> 00:12:37.789
If you don't like the decisions
Trump makes,

00:12:37.789 --> 00:12:39.091
then take it up with him.

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:41.159
Of course, in this case,
it's just easier

00:12:41.159 --> 00:12:44.196
to pretend Anthony Fauci is
president, not Donald Trump,

00:12:44.196 --> 00:12:45.630
because then you'd
have to acknowledge

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.300
that the horrific death toll
and the cratering economy

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.202
have unfolded under
Trump's watch.

00:12:50.202 --> 00:12:53.606
Instead, Fox News would rather
concoct an elaborate fantasy

00:12:53.606 --> 00:12:55.774
where Fauci is making
all the calls,

00:12:55.774 --> 00:12:58.010
while he has Trump tied
to a chair in a closet

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:00.045
with duct tape over his mouth.

00:13:00.045 --> 00:13:03.148
"Fauci! Let me go!
I see you, Fauci.

00:13:03.148 --> 00:13:04.917
You can't hide from me."

00:13:04.917 --> 00:13:06.818
As we've seen
from other countries,

00:13:06.818 --> 00:13:10.055
it's possible to have
an aggressive regime of testing,

00:13:10.055 --> 00:13:13.525
contact tracing, and social
distancing to keep people safe,

00:13:13.525 --> 00:13:15.059
while also making sure
they keep their paychecks

00:13:15.059 --> 00:13:16.562
and health insurance.

00:13:16.562 --> 00:13:18.830
But Trump and his allies have
no interest in any of that.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.032
They'd rather wish the virus
away and send working people

00:13:21.032 --> 00:13:23.068
back into the economy
like cannon fodder

00:13:23.068 --> 00:13:25.437
while they do their shows
in safe isolation.

00:13:25.437 --> 00:13:28.206
They don't care if otherwise
mild-mannered scientists

00:13:28.206 --> 00:13:30.942
are warning us that we're in...
-Deep [bleep].

00:13:30.942 --> 00:13:32.811
See, real book.

00:13:32.811 --> 00:13:34.346
This has been "A Closer Look."

